======================================================================
I. THE RAPIDITY METRIC SPACE
======================================================================

  Define d(m, n) = |rapidity(m) - rapidity(n)| = |ln(m) - ln(n)|/2
  = ln(max(m,n)/min(m,n))/2

  This is the LOG-RATIO METRIC. Two numbers are close iff their
  ratio is close to 1.

  d(n, n+1) = ln(1+1/n)/2 ~ 1/(2n). The gaps shrink.
  d(n, 2n)  = ln(2)/2 = 0.3466. CONSTANT! (one octave)
  d(n, 3n)  = ln(3)/2 = 0.5493. CONSTANT! (one twelfth)

  In this metric, MULTIPLICATION BY k is a TRANSLATION by ln(k)/2.
  The natural numbers under rapidity form a DISCRETE LOG-LATTICE.

  Rapidity distance matrix d(m,n) for m,n = 2,...,8:
           2    3    4    5    6    7    8
  2:    0.000  0.203  0.347  0.458  0.549  0.626  0.693
  3:    0.203  0.000  0.144  0.255  0.347  0.424  0.490
  4:    0.347  0.144  0.000  0.112  0.203  0.280  0.347
  5:    0.458  0.255  0.112  0.000  0.091  0.168  0.235
  6:    0.549  0.347  0.203  0.091  0.000  0.077  0.144
  7:    0.626  0.424  0.280  0.168  0.077  0.000  0.067
  8:    0.693  0.490  0.347  0.235  0.144  0.067  0.000

