III. THE WALLIS-LIKE RAPIDITY PRODUCT
======================================================================

  Wallis: pi/2 = prod (2k)^2/((2k-1)(2k+1))
  In rapidity: sum of rapidities = sum ln((2k)^2/((2k-1)(2k+1)))/2
  = sum [2*ln(2k) - ln(2k-1) - ln(2k+1)] / 2

  The prime Cayley product (from earlier session):
  prod_{p<=N} (p+1)/(p-1) ~ C * ln(N)^2
  In rapidity: sum_{p<=N} [ln(p+1) - ln(p-1)] / 2 ~ 2*ln(ln(N)) + const

  sum_{p<=  2} rapidity-of-Q(1/p) = 0.549306
  sum_{p<=  3} rapidity-of-Q(1/p) = 0.895880
  sum_{p<=  5} rapidity-of-Q(1/p) = 1.098612
